This directory is what the running containers read their policy from.

It is tracked so the bind mount always has a real directory to point at — an
absent source makes Docker invent a root-owned empty one, and the container
then fails to load a policy for a reason that looks like a permissions bug.

The policy files inside are deliberately NOT tracked (see .gitignore). That is
the whole point: config/ is a git working tree, and mounting it into a running
engine means every checkout, merge and branch switch silently reconfigures
production. Three distinct policy fingerprints appeared in the first shadow
window that way, none of them from anyone editing a policy.

Populate it deliberately:   make deploy_policy
See what is actually live:  make deploy_policy_status
